{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["וְתוֹלַעַת שָׁנִי — wool dyed red is called תולעת, and the dye is called שני. As it is written: (Nahum 2:4) אַנְשֵׁי חַיִל מְתֻלָּעִים — men of valor clothed in dyed garments. And likewise: הָאֲמֻנִים עָלֵינוּ תֹלַע — a dyed garment. And likewise it proves: אִם יִהְיוּ חֲטָאֵיכֶם כַּשָּׁנִים כַּשֶּׁלֶג יַלְבִּינוּ — if they grow red as תולע like wool they shall be — שני and snow are names of colors, one red and one white. But תולע and the wool are both wool, except that the תולע is dyed wool, while the wool is white without dye." "וְשֵׁשׁ — linen, but the other kinds are dyed wool." "וְעִזִּים — spun goat-hair."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:43:01.305111062Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}